<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Holocene Gasterosteus aculeatus cellular Turing wavelength (56 µm) — Model fidelity to source: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The script integrates the Schnakenberg PDE and evaluates the onset formula k_c² = γ (Dv f_u + Du g_v) / (2 Du Dv) for three values of a and for the equal-diffusion control, which is stable. Lean checks the cleared trace, determinant, discriminant and the analytic contraction. Deduction: a, Du, Dv and γ are chosen to place the Holocene carrier on the assigned 56 µm, and the stickleback papers are genetic rather than a published parameter table." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "datasets/gasterosteus_aculeatus_turing_wavelength_s0/gasterosteus_aculeatus_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json L78–L96: reconstructed parameters are labelled as such <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/4fdc4af8f8347d55b64a1de2f47c8a0931a60888/datasets/gasterosteus_aculeatus_turing_wavelength_s0/gasterosteus_aculeatus_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json#L78-L96>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Holocene Gasterosteus aculeatus cellular Turing wavelength (56 µm) — Morphometric validation: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass-1 remediation is in the code. Parabolic interpolation puts the Holocene nonlinear peak at 54.99 µm against the 56.00 µm reference (not equal). Absolute luminance < 95 separates specimen melanin area 0.266 from render 0.097. KS D is 0.685 versus the equal-diffusion field and 0.179 versus specimen luminance inside the mask. Sweep r = 0.9938 with RMSE 4.88 µm. Posterior r remains 0.372 because R4 forbids fitting that half. The benthic nonlinear peak (57.90 µm) misses the analytic 52.23 µm reference; that miss is the score cap." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "datasets/gasterosteus_aculeatus_turing_wavelength_s0/run_metrics.json L1–L45: R3 result: benthic nonlinear 57.90 does not sit below Holocene 54.99 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/4fdc4af8f8347d55b64a1de2f47c8a0931a60888/datasets/gasterosteus_aculeatus_turing_wavelength_s0/run_metrics.json#L1-L45>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-benthic-successor-nonlinear-cellular-wavelength>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-equal-diffusion-ablation-activator-standard-deviation>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-gamma-sweep-pearson-r-of-nonlinear-wavelength-versus-analytic-c>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-gamma-sweep-rmse-of-wavelength>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-held-out-posterior-flank-pearson-r-of-the-bar-envelope>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-holocene-nonlinear-cellular-wavelength-versus-analytic-k-c-target>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-ks-statistic-patterned-activator-versus-equal-diffusion-control>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-marine-predecessor-nonlinear-cellular-wavelength>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-body-area-fraction>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-mask-melanin-area-fraction-versus-rendered-composite>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-versus-render-luminance-ks-inside-the-body-mask>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Holocene Gasterosteus aculeatus cellular Turing wavelength (56 µm) — MorphoEval overall 86.3/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the same Schnakenberg carrier (Holocene analytic λ_c = 56.00 µm; marine 61.81 µm; benthic 52.23 µm). Parabolic radial-FFT interpolation moves the Holocene nonlinear peak to 54.99 µm. Gamma-sweep Pearson r is 0.9938 (RMSE 4.88 µm). Absolute luminance < 95 gives specimen melanin area 0.266 versus render 0.097. The saturated benthic peak is 57.90 µm, so the nonlinear lattice does not follow the analytic contraction. Posterior bar r stays 0.372 because that half was not fit. GIF cv_sim_similarity remains 88.4 at 960×548, 12 frames. Overall 86.3/100 (faithfulness 85.4, reproducibility 88.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 4fdc4af8f8347d55b64a1de2f47c8a0931a60888; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 86, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 91, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/gasterosteus_aculeatus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 4fdc4af8f8347d55b64a1de2f47c8a0931a60888, image/png, 544837 B, 1632×984 px, artifact_sha256 8d5a2170cfe64f0e92aa54fe40bd46d327d4a3ef9223006cb9677e6e090befb2 (sha256 8d5a2170cfe64f0e92aa54fe40bd46d327d4a3ef9223006cb9677e6e090befb2), spec_fingerprint 3db7c83138922a03aef82aaf803ecbe744b83029257f1146668b5acc01d7c2cb. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 3db7c83138922a03aef82aaf803ecbe744b83029257f1146668b5acc01d7c2cb; artifact_sha256: 8d5a2170cfe64f0e92aa54fe40bd46d327d4a3ef9223006cb9677e6e090befb2; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/gasterosteus_aculeatus_turing_wavelength_s0/gasterosteus_aculeatus_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=a53e439d8af1eeb7..., datasets/gasterosteus_aculeatus_turing_wavelength_s0/gasterosteus_aculeatus_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=69b13a9c5037e468..., datasets/gasterosteus_aculeatus_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=6e834bc83f029f3b..., datasets/gasterosteus_aculeatus_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=bc4c0aa8b21f50ae...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 diffusion-driven instability and a selected wavenumber | Schnakenberg 1979 two-species kinetics | Miller 2007 Kitlg cis-regulatory reduction of freshwater pigmentation | Greenwood 2011 genetic basis of juvenile stickleback pigment patterns | Tapanes & Rennison 2024 density and barring are different QTLs; reconstructed_in_script: Diffusion pair and gamma fixed so Holocene analytic λ_c equals the assigned 56 µm | Chronospecies knob a = 0.28 / 0.20 / 0.14 | Organ-scale bar cosine is fit on the anterior flank only; transfer_boundary: Nakamasu 2009 zebrafish pigment-cell interactions are not stickleback data; does_not_claim: That 56 µm is resolved by the Krisp photograph | That the nonlinear benthic FFT peak equals 52.23 µm | That plate number or Pitx1 is predicted." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Open: nonlinear benthic radial peak does not track analytic 52.23 µm. Not adjusted by changing a or the FFT window.",
        "remediation needed: Resolved R1: melanin area uses luminance < 95 (specimen 0.266, render 0.097).",
        "remediation needed: Resolved R2: dominant_wavelength_cells interpolates the radial peak.",
        "remediation needed: Resolved R3: re-measured peaks are marine 60.25, Holocene 54.99, benthic 57.90 µm. The saturated benthic pattern does not shorten past the Holocene peak.",
        "remediation needed: Resolved R4: posterior r remains 0.372; the posterior half is still not in the fit." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.63e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Holocene Gasterosteus aculeatus cellular Turing wavelength (56 µm) — Parameter expressivity: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Raising γ from 3 to 10 shortens both analytic and nonlinear wavelengths (Pearson r = 0.9938). Setting Du = Dv collapses the activator standard deviation from 0.807 to ~0. Changing a from 0.28 to 0.20 to 0.14 shortens analytic λ from 61.81 to 56.00 to 52.23 µm. The saturated benthic FFT peak does not follow that last step (57.90 µm), which is reported rather than tuned away." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

